\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 This method is for Mach platforms only\'d0it is not defined for other platforms. The standard unit used to measure a paper\'27s dimensions is a point (for example, NSPrintInfo defines a paper\'27s size in points). However, the user can select a different unit of measurement from the NSPageLayout panel. Use this method to get the ratio between a point and the currently selected unit of measurement. Unless this method is invoked by \b pickedUnits:\b0  both \i old\i0  and \i new\i0  will be set to the same ratio value.\
\fs14\
\fs28 The \b pickedUnits:\b0  method is invoked when the user selects a new unit of measurement from the NSPageLayout panel. Subclasses should override the \b pickedUnits:\b0  method to update any controls, located on the accessory view, that display dimensional values. Use this method to get the old and new ratios. See \b pickedUnits:\b0  for details.\
\fs14\
