\fs14\
\fs28 Subclasses should override this method to update controls in the accessory view that contain unit values. The ratios returned by the \b convertOldFactor:newFactor:\b0  method should be used to calculate the new values as shown below, where \b myField\b0  is an NSTextField located on the accessory view that needs to be updated:\
\fs14\
\pard \s20 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx2413 \tx2889 \tx3421 \tx3953 \tx4457 \tx4933 \tx7005 \tx7509 \tx8013 \tx8517 \tx9021 \tx9525 \tx10029 \tx10533 \tx11037 \tx11513 \f2 \fs24 - pickedUnitsLsender\
\{\
\tab float old, new;\
\
\tab /* At this point the units have been selected but not set. */\
\tab [self convertOldFactor:&old newFactor:&new];\
\
\tab /* Update myField based on the conversion factors. */\
\tab [myField setFloatValue:([myField floatValue]*new/old)];\
\
\tab /* Set the selected units. */\
\tab return [super pickedUnits:sender];\
\}\
\fs14\
